# A function assigned to the prototype object of a constructor function is a fixed member when the store has written it before anything looks the name up.
# The store counts only if it has written the member whenever it completes, and every lookup by name counts that may start at an object below the holder.
# Fixed: a strict store, a sloppy store to a holder that nobody freezes, a store under a computed key that is one name, and a holder whose instance escapes and is read as the unknown object after the store.
# Not fixed: a sloppy store to a frozen holder completes without storing. A store under one of two keys writes one of them. Object.assign copies what its source has at that time.
# A setter above the holder that one path defines takes the value. An instance that has escaped comes back as the unknown object, and the name is looked up on it before the store.
# RUN: flow
# CHECK: layout L0 flow={{*}} namedMembers=[{key="m" function=f10 mutability=Fixed
# CHECK: layout L1 flow={{*}} namedMembers=[{key="m" function=f10 mutability=Fixed
# CHECK: layout L2 flow={{*}} namedMembers=[{key="m" function=f10 mutability=Fixed
# CHECK: layout L3 flow={{*}} namedMembers=[{key="m" function=f10 mutability=Fixed
# CHECK: layout L4 flow=
# CHECK-NOT: mutability=Fixed
# CHECK: layout L5 flow=
# CHECK-NOT: mutability=Fixed
# CHECK: layout L6 flow=
# CHECK-NOT: mutability=Fixed
# CHECK: layout L7 flow=
# CHECK-NOT: mutability=Fixed
# CHECK: layout L8 flow=
# CHECK-NOT: mutability=Fixed
# CHECK: layout L9 

